    {
      "text": "came wise men from the east to Jerusalem, Matt. 2:1. whosoever heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them, I will liken him unto a wise man, Matt. 7:24 (3 Ne. 14:24). be ye therefore wise as serpents, Matt. 10:16 (D&C 111:11). thou hast hid these things from the wise, Matt. 11:25 (Luke 10:21). a faithful and wise servant, Matt. 24:45 (Luke 12:42; JS—M 1:49). five of them were wise, Matt. 25:2. children of this world are in their generation wiser, Luke 16:8. debtor … both to the wise, and to the unwise, Rom. 1:14. Professing themselves to be wise, they became fools, Rom. 1:22. lest ye should be wise in your own conceits, Rom. 11:25 (12:16). I would have you wise unto that which is good, Rom. 16:19. Where is the wise, 1 Cor. 1:20. foolishness of God is wiser than men, 1 Cor. 1:25. chosen the foolish things of the world to confound the wise, 1 Cor. 1:27. Lord knoweth the thoughts of the wise, 1 Cor. 3:20. walk … not as fools, but as wise, Eph. 5:15. be ye not unwise, but understanding, Eph. 5:17. immortal, invisible, the only wise God, 1 Tim. 1:17. holy scriptures, which are able to make thee wise, 2 Tim. 3:15. Who is a wise man … among you, James 3:13.",
